# Godot (its cache is per machine, except the list of native extensions to load: without it a
# fresh checkout opens with Terrain3D unregistered and its editor plugin fails to parse)
**/.godot/*
!**/.godot/extension_list.cfg
*.import.tmp
export/
build/
# The built world. What the game reads at run time is tracked, so a clone plays without Python:
#   game/world/generated/{world_manifest.json, pois.json, roads.json, rivers.json}
#   game/world/generated/runtime/   the 1024 copies of heights, regions, water and water level
#   game/world/generated/cells/     one JSON per 256 m cell: scatter, landmarks, encounters
#   game/terrain_data/terrain3d*.res   Terrain3D's sixteen regions
# (game/world/terrain_assets.tres is tracked too.) Everything else the builder writes -- the
# full-resolution heights, colour, control, flow, texture, water and region maps, 300 MB that only
# the terrain import reads -- stays out, and so does anything new it starts writing until a rule
# here says otherwise. `./run.sh world` writes them all again. See README.md, "Run it".
game/world/generated/*
!game/world/generated/world_manifest.json
!game/world/generated/pois.json
!game/world/generated/roads.json
!game/world/generated/rivers.json
!game/world/generated/runtime/
!game/world/generated/cells/
game/terrain_data/*
!game/terrain_data/terrain3d*.res
# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
# Tools output
captures/
tools/out/
# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# local tool state
.claude/worktrees/
captures_prev/

# a warning census writes it for one run of Godot (tools/debug/warning_census.py)
game/override.cfg
# each checkout's own user:// for tests and tools (tools/godot_env.sh)
.godot_user/
